      {
        "id": "p12-cont-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Now try $37\\times13\\times3$. Can you predict the value of $37\\times17\\times3$? Can you explain what happens?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1443$ and $1887$. The outer digits match the middle factor; each inner digit is the sum of those outer digits.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}37\\times13\\times3&=111\\times13\\\\37\\times13\\times3&=1110+333\\\\37\\times13\\times3&=1443\\\\37\\times17\\times3&=111\\times17\\\\37\\times17\\times3&=1110+777\\\\37\\times17\\times3&=1887\\end{align*}$$\nThe outer digits are $1$ and $3$, or $1$ and $7$, matching $13$ or $17$. Each inner digit is respectively $1+3=4$ or $1+7=8$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
