        "answer": {
          "short": "$11\\,111=41\\times271$.\n\nSample problem: Find $41\\times13\\times271$ and predict $41\\times17\\times271$. Answers: $144\\,443$ and $188\\,887$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}41\\times271&=41\\times(270+1)\\\\41\\times271&=11\\,070+41\\\\41\\times271&=11\\,111\\end{align*}$$\nThus $41$ is a factor of $11\\,111$; choose $b=271$.\n\nSample problem: Find $41\\times13\\times271$ and predict $41\\times17\\times271$. Explain the pattern.\n$$\\begin{align*}41\\times13\\times271&=11\\,111\\times13\\\\41\\times13\\times271&=111\\,110+33\\,333\\\\41\\times13\\times271&=144\\,443\\\\41\\times17\\times271&=11\\,111\\times17\\\\41\\times17\\times271&=111\\,110+77\\,777\\\\41\\times17\\times271&=188\\,887\\end{align*}$$\nThe outer digits match $13$ or $17$; each of the four inner digits is respectively $1+3=4$ or $1+7=8$.",
